#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# jacobi_zn

#% text
# `jacobi_zn(u, m)` gives the Jacobi zeta function `Z(u | m) = E(am(u | m) | m) - E(m)*u/K(m)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 22.16.32. `Z` is odd in `u` and periodic with period `2*K(m)`; it vanishes at `u = 0` and `u = K(m)`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
jacobi_zn(0.5, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.11638850054726674

#% cell
jacobi_zn(1.0, 0.9)
#% output
#= 0.35386282791233

#% cell
jacobi_zn(elliptic_k(0.5), 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The definition:

#% cell
jacobi_zn(0.7, 0.4) - (jacobi_epsilon(0.7, 0.4) - elliptic_e(0.4)*0.7/elliptic_k(0.4))
#% output
#= 0.0

